       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum of 2,550 mg/day (about 1,000 mg per dose). A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and severe GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day in divided doses**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n- **Another dose**, such as 500 mg or 1,000 mg\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and I'll enter it with a note saying the dose was confirmed. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
